\n" [:option {:value "959"} "10,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "960"} "Allround, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "963"} "1928"] "\n" [:option {:value "977"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "991"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "995"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "999"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "1003"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "1007"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "1015"} "1964"] "\n" [:option {:value "1023"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "1031"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "1040"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "1049"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "1058"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "1067"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "1077"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "1087"} "1994"] "\n" [:option {:value "1099"} "1998"] "\n" [:option {:value "1113"} "2002"] "\n" [:option {:value "1127"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "924505"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350649"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "9001030"} "2018"] "\n" [:option {:value "19020403"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15001103"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/533"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "5,000 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "26 January 1924 — 10:00"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/25"} "Stade Olympique, Chamonix"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/958"} "22 from 10 countries"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Starter"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002409"} "Hans Valär"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]]] [:tr {:class "referees", :style ""} [:th {} "Referee"] [:td {:style "width: 400px"} [:a {:href "/athletes/5002404"} "Hans Oscar Hammerstad"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Attendance"] [:td {} "1,342"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Only a few 5,000 metres performances under nine minutes had been posted prior to the Games. At their Davos training races, " [:a {:href "/athletes/97613"} "Julius Skutnabb"] " (8:50.4) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/98260"} "Clas Thunberg"] " (8:51.9) had recorded the fastest times of the season. Three of the four Norwegians in competition also had sub-9 minute performances listed, all skated at a Frogner meet shortly before the Olympics, World Record holder " [:a {:href "/athletes/97911"} "Harald Strøm"] " being the fastest, with 8:52.3."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The second competition of the day got underway with the first two pairs being rescheduled due to non-starters. " [:a {:href "/athletes/86149"} "Charlie Gorman"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/96670"} "Léon Quaglia"] " were the first to hit the ice. Quaglia had won the French Championships at the same rink two weeks earlier, and he improved on his performance in the 5000 m by more than 15 seconds, with 9.08.6. The first to go under nine minutes was " [:a {:href "/athletes/96250"} "Frithjof Paulsen"] " of Norway, followed by his compatriot Harald Strøm, who listed 8:54.6. Strøm’s time was good, considering that he had caught the flu on the previous day. As the " [:a {:href "/flagbearers?edition_id=29"} "Norwegian flag bearer"] ", he had been out in the rain for hours wearing nothing but his race outfit."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The strongest North American distance skater, " [:a {:href "/athletes/84104"} "Valentine Bialas"] ", was coupled with Julius Skutnabb, and delivered an interesting fight won by the 34-year-old Finn, who also improved the season’s best time to 8:48.4. His teammate Thunberg did not have such a strong competitor in his race, but that did not stop him from outclassing the rest of the field with 8:39.0. The two remaining Norwegians, " [:a {:href "/athletes/89436"} "Roald Larsen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/95517"} "Sigurd Moen"] ", both delivered fine performances, but were also unable to approach the leading Finnish duo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Thunberg was one of the dominant speed skaters of the era. He only started skating at age 20, but managed to win five World Championships and four European titles. One of his nicknames was “The Nurmi of the ice”, which he considered somewhat insulting, as he thought " [:a {:href "/athletes/67728"} "Paavo Nurmi"] " might as well be called the “Thunberg of the track”."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button287293", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button287293').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "600 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1000 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1400 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "1800 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2600 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3000 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3400 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3800 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "4200 m"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "4600 m"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [: